399
00:29:31,559 --> 00:29:32,660
Military headquarters runs a tight ship.

400
00:29:33,039 --> 00:29:34,460
Every military vehicle's movement is logged.

401
00:29:34,500 --> 00:29:35,519
But they can't be lent out privately.

402
00:29:36,039 --> 00:29:36,640
So I got the idea

403
00:29:36,740 --> 00:29:38,160
to look into the records of vehicles

404
00:29:38,319 --> 00:29:38,819
that transported soldiers from

405
00:29:38,819 --> 00:29:40,460
the Xiping battlefield to the mines.

406
00:29:41,180 --> 00:29:42,339
Though they doctored the destination,

407
00:29:42,440 --> 00:29:44,240
the time, distance, and headcount

408
00:29:44,539 --> 00:29:46,000
all match up perfectly.

409
00:29:46,440 --> 00:29:47,160
And the order came from

410
00:29:47,839 --> 00:29:49,240
Feng Sanli, commander of the 4th Brigade,

411
00:29:49,660 --> 00:29:50,339
2nd Army.

412
00:29:53,059 --> 00:29:54,039
Great.

413
00:29:54,240 --> 00:29:54,779
Xueting,

414
00:29:55,420 --> 00:29:56,279
I'll get this article

415
00:29:56,460 --> 00:29:58,880
typeset and printed right away.

416
00:29:59,279 --> 00:30:01,460
Publish it through the underground press.

417
00:30:30,740 --> 00:30:31,339
Hello?

418
00:30:31,619 --> 00:30:32,259
General Mou.

419
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:33,500
This is Hongwen.

420
00:30:34,019 --> 00:30:34,920
The man

421
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:36,140
I once trusted in Japan

422
00:30:36,339 --> 00:30:38,000
has gone deep into the Yu Army

423
00:30:38,079 --> 00:30:39,759
and found solid evidence.

424
00:30:40,160 --> 00:30:41,779
He'll expose it under the pen name

425
00:30:42,079 --> 00:30:42,960
Junguan.

426
00:30:43,680 --> 00:30:44,539
Junguan?

427
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:46,420
From "A gentleman dies, but his cap stays on"?

428
00:30:48,299 --> 00:30:49,400
This man has grand ambitions.

429
00:30:50,140 --> 00:30:50,960
These days,

430
00:30:51,660 --> 00:30:52,599
these hot-blooded young writers

431
00:30:52,599 --> 00:30:53,660
with their pens are no less powerful

432
00:30:54,119 --> 00:30:55,839
than machine guns and heavy artillery.

433
00:30:56,559 --> 00:30:57,259
Tomorrow

434
00:30:58,279 --> 00:31:00,700
this will be all over town.

435
00:31:01,619 --> 00:31:02,380
Very good.

436
00:31:16,319 --> 00:31:18,460
Papers! Get your papers!

437
00:31:18,700 --> 00:31:19,500
That's so cruel.

438
00:31:20,319 --> 00:31:21,160
What is this world coming to?

439
00:31:21,599 --> 00:31:22,339
That's just too much.

440
00:31:22,500 --> 00:31:23,319
What hope is there left?

441
00:31:23,319 --> 00:31:23,859
Right?

442
00:31:23,859 --> 00:31:24,660
Is there any law anymore?

443
00:31:24,940 --> 00:31:26,200
The Yu Army forcing soldiers

444
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:26,960
to work as miners?

445
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:28,960
50 soldiers died in a mining disaster?

446
00:31:29,779 --> 00:31:30,539
That's just too much.

447
00:31:32,039 --> 00:31:33,160
That's 50 men.

448
00:31:38,039 --> 00:31:39,019
This is

449
00:31:39,019 --> 00:31:39,960
all over town now.

450
00:31:39,960 --> 00:31:40,559
Exactly.

451
00:31:41,079 --> 00:31:41,500
This is a toughie.

452
00:31:41,579 --> 00:31:42,680
We need to find a way to suppress it.

453
00:31:49,779 --> 00:31:50,339
Young Master.

454
00:31:53,140 --> 00:31:54,460
The underground press has been burned down.

455
00:31:54,920 --> 00:31:56,400
But they only handled the printing.

456
00:31:56,500 --> 00:31:57,920
They don't know where the articles came from.

457
00:31:58,460 --> 00:31:59,740
The manuscripts we brought back

458
00:32:00,119 --> 00:32:00,660
were compared

459
00:32:00,660 --> 00:32:01,900
against the handwriting

460
00:32:01,900 --> 00:32:02,680
of all military clerical staff.

461
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:03,960
Still no leads

462
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:05,839
